    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena tied a stone to a thread and counted its swings.\n\"It swings at a steady rate,\" she said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "pendulum",
     "oscillation",
     "time period"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A simple pendulum is a small weight called a bob hung from a thread. One oscillation is when the bob goes from one side to the other and back. The time for one oscillation is the time period.\nThe time period depends on the length of the thread: a longer thread has a longer time period. It does not depend on the mass of the bob.\nThe SI unit of time is the second. Pendulum clocks used this steady swing to keep time."
    }
   },
